    {
      "name": "Booby Traps",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "reaction",
        "description": "<p>When a PC fails an action roll to navigate the dungeon, activate a trap or hazard such as a spike pit, gauntlet of swinging blades, or locked room slowly filling with water. The party must succeed on a group action roll to deactivate, disarm, or escape it. On a failure, each PC involved in the group action roll takes <strong>2d6+3</strong> physical or magic damage (GM's choice).</p><section id=\"secret-ORvRK15fEmVPMhNn\" class=\"secret\"><p>What kinds of traps and hazards fill this dungeon? What does their construction tell you about whoever designed them? Have any of them been triggered prior to the party's arrival?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
